WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.571
On the morning this picture was posted, my microscope

00:00:03.571 --> 00:00:06.693
stood at home in Qatar. There is nothing spectacular

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:09.121
about the room. That was the point.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.840
I bought it near Qasr El Einy in Cairo. Transporting it

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.832
to Qatar was a nuisance, but I could now examine

00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:25.827
specimens beyond scheduled laboratory hours.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:34.317
I wanted to be able to return to an observation when

00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:37.480
the question occurred to me, not only during scheduled

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.183
laboratory hours.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.205
University instruments came with protocols and

00:00:46.205 --> 00:00:49.878
calendars, for good reasons. I valued that training,

00:00:49.878 --> 00:00:52.633
but curiosity kept its own hours.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.969
The photograph shows a vacation morning: books, notes

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.927
and an American Chemical Society mug. No supervisor was

00:01:03.927 --> 00:01:05.687
waiting for a result.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:13.075
At home, I could come back to the same object another

00:01:13.075 --> 00:01:16.371
day. I could spend time looking, change my mind, and

00:01:16.371 --> 00:01:17.030
look again.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.601
A microscope lets you see. Explanation still needs

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:28.751
controls, methods and evidence that other people can

00:01:28.751 --> 00:01:32.689
examine. I had a place to practice the first part.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.215
It stood there on my desk, among the ordinary objects

00:01:40.215 --> 00:01:43.228
of a morning at home. Scientific attention had

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:45.111
somewhere to live between classes.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.011
An instrument at home cannot replace a research

00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:56.572
laboratory. Mine let me begin questions before anybody

00:01:56.572 --> 00:01:57.907
assigned an experiment.
